diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 7fdfd999e..52f704ecb 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ See [Full exhaustive changes (very long)](/README.md#full-exhaustive-very-long-a
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5298+) **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).
 - **Performance & code cleanup:** Broad Python/XML/C++ optimizations (e.g., removed giant ConfigObj docstring (see [KI#21.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#215---addressed--fixed---removed-the-giant-configobj-docstring-very-inefficiently-in-the-python-code-and-commented-out-most-if-not-all-as-well)); cached hot values via `static const`/hoisting; normalized inconsistent asset names (see for example [KI#18](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#18---very-inconsistent-naming-in-some-assets))), **map-type heaviness caching** (`CvGame::recomputeMapnameHeaviness`) so land/naval checks run once per game (feeds UNITAI tuning) (see [KI#42](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#42---enhancedaddressed-tune-ais-preferred-based-unitai-based-on-war-status-offense-mode-defense-mode-combined-power-ratios-of-ennemies-etc-if-any-other-general-sanity-checks-and-efficiency-city-size-map-type-land-heavy-vs-water-heavy-vs-other-if-any-for-example-general-suicide-or-such-tendencies-etc), **bonus-specific builds/improvements caching** (e.g. `CvUnitAI::getBonusSpecificLandBuilds`), [AI Personality Panel performance optimization notes](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching)), **feature-level caching** (AI Personality Panel), refactor **extremely redundant code** (e.g. `refreshUnitSelection` in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)), cache redundant computation (e.g. **store per turn and player** top cities' values `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`), etc.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5314+) **Found-value** evaluation now uses **`int`** end-to-end (CitySiteEvaluator, AIFoundValue, CvPlot cache, SPI, Python callback), **not `short`**. Why: **avoid overflow/underflow** and short wraparounds in site scoring; keep the logic the same while **improving reliability**. Expectation: more robust site values, fewer edge-case penalties/boosts from short overflow; no known negative gameplay change. Performance: `int` is typically at least as fast as short on modern CPUs; no slowdown expected. Tested: autoplay ran fine. See [Change from short to int the Found value pipeline](/README.md#change-from-short-to-int-the-found-value-pipeline).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5335+) Removed the old clunky Base AdvCiv's `CONCEPT_TRAIT` XML clutter. Now using using the more efficient `WIDGET_PYTHON` similarly instead.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5335+) Removed the old clunky Base AdvCiv's `CONCEPT_TRAIT` XML clutter. Now using the more efficient `WIDGET_PYTHON` similarly instead.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5348+) **Cache once per session precomputed** Sevopedia Traits' Charts and Sevopedia Improvements' Weights (Leaders) Chart on category open before any entry is clicked on. This uses a simplified version of the AI Personality Panel's caching approach. See [AI Personality panel caching](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching).
 - **Load Precomputed Files**: optionally load the Sevopedia Leader's **AI Personality Panel**'s information to display as a **predumped** file ([SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/SevoPediaLeaderCachePredumped.py)): (~550k Python literal characters) (default ON, recommended): since these values never change for players, this is more efficient. For modders, if they change leader XML info values, they can turn the SAS define to always compute temporarily so they can regenerate then update the file, or permanently for quick testing or if they prefer.
 - **External File Opening**: Access from Civ4 ingame local files in the system on Windows. See [KI#87](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#87---fixed-and-generalized-cannot-open-bug-mod-help-engchm-on-windows-in-advciv-sas-but-can-open-it-on-windows-in-base-advciv-even-though-path-is-the-same)
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - Added **Emojis** without having to tediously implement them as characters. See [Emojis](/README.md#emojis) and [CIV4ArtDefines_Interface.xml](/Assets/XML/Art/CIV4ArtDefines_Interface.xml).
